## 4. Internal Data Models

### 4.1 Artifact Metadata (Internal)

Used during filtering stages before content is loaded.

```json
{
  "title": "ArtifactMetadata",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["id", "source", "domain", "category", "title", "tags", "updated_at"],
  "properties": {
    "id": { "type": "string" },
    "source": { "type": "string" },
    "domain": { "type": "string" },
    "category": { "type": "string" },
    "title": { "type": "string" },
    "tags": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string" }
    },
    "updated_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time"
    },
    "priority": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0
    },
    "token_estimate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0
    }
  }
}
```

### 4.2 Artifact Content (Internal)

Full artifact with content after late materialization.

```json
{
  "title": "ArtifactContent",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["id", "source", "domain", "category", "title", "content", "token_count"],
  "properties": {
    "id": { "type": "string" },
    "source": { "type": "string" },
    "domain": { "type": "string" },
    "category": { "type": "string" },
    "title": { "type": "string" },
    "content": { "type": "string" },
    "token_count": { "type": "integer" },
    "metadata": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true
    }
  }
}
```

---

## 5. Environment Variables

Configuration can be overridden via environment variables:

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `CULL_HOST` | 0.0.0.0 | Server bind address |
| `CULL_PORT` | 3003 | Server port |
| `CULL_WORKERS` | 4 | Number of worker processes |
| `CULL_LOG_LEVEL` | INFO | Logging level |
| `CULL_LOG_FORMAT` | json | Logging format (json/text) |
| `CULL_CONFIG_DIR` | /etc/cull | Configuration directory |
| `CULL_DEFAULT_BUDGET` | 8000 | Default token budget |
| `CULL_DEFAULT_RULES` | default | Default priority rules |

